ve fiber layer (E) is the outermost layer of the retina, containing the axons of ganglion cells, which can be identified in an OCT image.\n\nStep 4: Select the most appropriate option based on the analysis.\n- Given the characteristics of the options and the context of the OCT image, the most appropriate option is E. Retinal nerve fiber layer.\n- This layer is directly visible in the OCT image and is a critical component of the retina.\n- The other options, while plausible, are", "answer": null}
